 "notes": "The hook headline builds on the spoken words and the 3D card lands in the breath. Each body scene has one hero with its top between y 280 and 340 and one or two elements that land on their key word. Real screenshots back b3, b4 and b8, and the b8 install pill overlaps the window above y 960 to keep the right rail clear. The b7 ticks land near colors, reviews and then codes. The CTA follows the Branding rules. | text: Long chunks split to stay under the 620 px line (about 18 characters). Script emphasis that isn't spoken moves to the spoken word: #D97757 to terracotta, 1,134,112 to million. \"Reviews the layout\" became \"Reviews\" because the script never says layout. | transitions: Mostly fade-blur (5 of 10). The two falls go into calm beats (the stake and the payoff), the two pushes go where the story turns, and there is one cut, into the install step. No non-default type appears twice in a row.",
